---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import F from '../../data/fees.json';
const groups = ['Business permits', 'Markets and cess', 'Parking', 'Buildings and land', 'Health', 'Other'];
const pick = ['Small trader shop', 'Hawker', 'Posho mill', 'Boda', 'Matatu', 'Banana', 'Slaughter', 'Food handler'];
---
<Base title="Fees you pay">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Learn" title="Fees you pay" lead="What the county may legally charge residents and traders, from the Nyamira County Finance Act, 2025." crumbs={[{ href: '/learn/', label: 'Learn' }, { href: '/learn/fees/', label: 'Fees you pay' }]} />
  <div class="stack-lg" style="margin-top:16px">
    <div class="panel stack">
      <p><strong>The law:</strong> <a href={F.act.url} rel="noopener">{F.act.name}</a>. Signed into law on 17 October 2025 and published in the Kenya Gazette on 22 December 2025. It applies from FY2025/26.</p>
      <p><strong>Zones:</strong> many fees depend on where you trade. <strong>Zone A</strong> is Nyamira and Keroka municipalities and Nyansiongo township. <strong>Zone B</strong> covers the market centres such as Kemera, Magombo, Ekerenyo, Manga, Gesima, Magwagwa and Tombe. <strong>Zone C</strong> is everywhere else.</p>
      <p class="small muted">If an officer asks for more than the Act allows, ask for an official receipt and the fee item in the Act. You can complain to the county revenue office or the Ombudsman (see <a href="/government/watchdogs/">Watchdogs</a>).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sw" lang="sw">
      <span class="eyebrow">Muhtasari kwa Kiswahili</span>
      <p>Ada zote za kaunti zimewekwa na Sheria ya Fedha ya Kaunti ya Nyamira, 2025. Ada nyingi hutegemea eneo (Zone A, B au C). Daima omba risiti rasmi.</p>
    </div>

    {groups.map((g) => {
      const rows = F.fees.filter((f) => f.group === g);
      return rows.length > 0 && (
        <details open={g === 'Business permits' || g === 'Markets and cess'}>
          <summary>{g} ({rows.length})</summary>
          <div class="table-box">
            <table class="cards">
              <thead><tr><th>Item (as written in the Act)</th><th>Fee</th><th>Per</th><th>Where in the Act</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>{rows.map((f) => (<tr><td>{f.item}</td><td data-label="Fee"><strong>{f.amountText}</strong></td><td data-label="Per">{f.unit}</td><td class="small muted" data-label="Act">{f.schedule}, {f.page}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </details>
      );
    })}

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>Good to know</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Produce cess is charged per vehicle by load (KSh 500 up to 1 tonne, 1,000 for 1–3 tonnes, 2,000 above 3 tonnes), not per bag.</li>
        <li>Boda boda parking is now a seasonal ticket (KSh 900 for 3 months, 1,500 for 6 months, 2,400 a year), replacing the old KSh 300 a month.</li>
        <li>Hospital charges follow the Social Health Authority (SHA) package. Some listed amounts are SHA rates, not what you pay in cash.</li>
        <li>Fees not listed in the 2025 Act stay at their earlier rates (section 21).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <p class="updated">Checked 22 Oct 2026. We could not confirm whether a 2026 Finance Bill is before the Assembly.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
